Step2: go to root user and install docker
       sudo -i
       yum install docker -y && systemctl start docker && systemctl enable docker
Step3: install minikube on amazon linux--->copy and paste commands
       curl -LO https://github.com/kubernetes/minikube/releases/latest/download/minikube-linux-amd64
sudo install minikube-linux-amd64 /usr/local/bin/minikube && rm minikube-linux-amd64

       minikube version

    start the minikube: 
minikube start --driver=docker --force
minikube status

Step4: kubectl is a cli tool which is used to interact with Kubernetes cluster

       install kubectl tool as well for ---->install kubectl on amazon Linux

    curl -LO "https://dl.k8s.io/release/$(curl -L -s https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable.txt)/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl"
    chmod +x kubectl
  mv kubectl /usr/local/bin
  kubectl version

Step5: create a pod, 2 types are there, Real time we are using Declarative only

a) imperative (command line)

kubectl run mypod --image nginx

kubectl get pods

b) Declarative (Manifest file)

vim pod.yml

how to check version: kubectl api-resources or kubectl api-resource | grep -i pod

---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: pod-1
spec:
  containers:
    - name: app-container
      image: shaikmustafa/dm
